# The lapsed login class: a member whose payment window closed with nothing
# recorded, or whose renewal failed, keeps reading mail and keeps their published
# pages, while sending from the address stops.
#
# On-box path: /etc/login.conf.d/lapsed. scripts/lapse-user.sh installs this
# drop-in and assigns it with `usermod -L lapsed <username>`, and the reverse run
# assigns the member class again. login.conf.d/<class> takes precedence over the
# same class in /etc/login.conf, the convention the member and hello classes
# already use here.
#
# `auth-smtp=reject` refuses submission authentication while IMAP finds no
# auth-imap capability, falls back to the default `auth` list and keeps working
# with the stored password. Dovecot and smtpd read the class on each attempt, so
# nothing has to be restarted. cap_mkdb(1) has to run after an edit whenever
# /etc/login.conf.db exists; the script does that.
#
# Upload and push are not this class's: both the sftp and git-shell sessions sit
# behind sshd's `Match Group members`, so the same script empties the secondary
# groups and the member keeps their key and their vhosts.
lapsed:auth-smtp=reject:tc=default:
